  "extraction_notes": "Figure shows a generic peptide-coupling scope using catalyst D (structure not shown in this panel), so catalyst D SMILES is left empty. The generic product 5 is represented with wildcard substituents for the two amino-acid side chains and ester group. Amino ester 4 is shown as the hydrochloride salt; product examples all use benzyl phenylalaninate as the amine partner (entry a). Histidine Tr protecting group interpreted as trityl-like aryl protecting group attached to imidazole nitrogen as drawn; exact positional assignment on the imidazole ring is based on best reading of the figure."
